    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-29T09:18:23+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-29T09:18:23+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-28T23:48:23Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-28T23:48:23Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred to the northeast of Tasmania extends a ridge over the southeast of the continent. This high and ridge will move eastwards over the Tasman Sea in coming days. A series of slow moving troughs will enter the west of the state today then move across the state on Wednesday and Thursday as a couple of cold fronts will move across waters to the south. A new high pressure system will become established south of the Bight during Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-29T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-28T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to high 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:40am to 3:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending north to northwesterly 25 to 40 km/h in the morning then tending north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers south of Yunta, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of raised dust north of Leigh Creek in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds northerly 25 to 35 km/h increasing to 30 to 45 km/h during the morning then shifting south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Leigh Creek in the morning and afternoon. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
